SUMMARY:Strings: Lorenzo Grimaldi – One-loop self-energy of Type II heavy
  string states
LOCATION:Room 226
DESCRIPTION:Lorenzo Grimaldi (Tor Vergata University of Rome\, Italy)\n\nOn
 e-loop self-energy of Type II heavy string states\n\nThe free string spect
 rum is highly degenerate\, with a degeneracy that grows exponentially with
  the mass\, making highly excited strings natural candidates for black-hol
 e microstates in the string/black-hole correspondence. A non-vanishing str
 ing coupling $g_s$ makes massive states unstable and shifts their masses\,
  partially lifting this degeneracy. At one loop\, the imaginary part of th
 e self-energy gives the tree-level width for the decay into two lower-mass
  states\, whereas the real part gives the mass shift and is generally IR-d
 ivergent. We firstly focus on the states of maximal spin at each level in 
 the NS-NS sector of Type II theories\, for which the analysis simplifies b
 ecause they cannot mix with other states. Exploiting elliptic functions\, 
 we obtain a closed-form expression for the worldsheet integral on the toru
 s. We then regularize and renormalize the remaining modular integral via t
 he $i\\varepsilon$-prescription\, extracting mass shifts and decay widths 
 up to level $N=10$.\n\nhttps://www.ceico.cz/seminars/archive/2026/#2026-11
 -30-lorenzo-grimaldi
URL:https://www.ceico.cz/seminars/archive/2026/#2026-11-30-lorenzo-grimaldi
END:VEVENT
